Venetium 0025 - Windows ARM32 build-fix round: the 17 compile failures of the first full ARM32 chrome build.

BATCH-ARM-1 section 5. His decisions (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md, "section 5 build - fix round", 2026-10-03): one patch; the fxdiv
workaround is logged first in TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES.md (B3); SwiftShader-off here completes 0021; cpuinfo is ported but reports only the
ARMv7 baseline; the installer suffix and the SODA indicator take arm names (Live Caption / SODA is not available on ARM32 - Google
ships no Windows ARM32 SODA). The full build (ninja -k 0 chrome, 16 h, 77,889 / 79,766 steps) stopped on 17 objects. 14 files:
- base/profiler/register_context_registers.h: Windows ARM32 (ARCH_CPU_ARMEL) branches - Sp, R11 (the Windows-on-ARM frame
  pointer), Pc. The sampling profiler stays off on 32-bit Windows as on x86 (StackSampler::Create returns nullptr); 4 objects
  (stack_copier_suspend, native_unwinder_win, stack_sampler, chrome renderer v8_unwinder) stopped on its #error.
- chrome/renderer/v8_unwinder.cc: on Windows ARM32 base::RegisterContext is ::CONTEXT, whose callee-saved registers are named
  R4..R10; ARM_CALLEE_SAVED_REGISTER picks that name there and arm_r4..arm_r10 on Linux/Android (unchanged).
- v8/src/base/platform/time.cc, time.h: Windows ARM32 takes the Windows-on-Arm ThreadTicks path (GetThreadTimes, no TSC, no
  __rdtsc) - the change 0017 made in base/time/time_win.cc.
- v8/src/libsampler/sampler.cc: Windows ARM32 register state (Pc, Sp, R11, Lr) instead of the x86 Eip/Esp/Ebp fallback.
- third_party/skia/src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h: Windows ARM32 leaves the pcs("aapcs-vfp") ABI branch (clang rejects pcs for
  Windows targets, an error under -Werror) and takes the _MSC_VER branch as Windows ARM64 does - narrow stages either way, and
  Windows on ARM always uses AAPCS-VFP (TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES, Chromium-side quirks).
- third_party/fxdiv/src/include/fxdiv.h: clang skips the _MulUnsignedHigh branch (TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES B3: undeclared on every clang
  target) for the portable branch, which rt2.1 compiles to the same single umull as MSVC's intrinsic (4 pthreadpool objects).
- ui/gfx/BUILD.gn: gfx depends on //extensions/buildflags and //third_party/widevine/cdm:buildflags. Supermium's
  paint_vector_icon.cc (ui_part_2.patch) includes chrome/common/chrome_paths.h, which includes both generated headers; in the V8
  snapshot toolchain (clang_x86_v8_arm) nothing ordered them before gfx.
- ui/gl/BUILD.gn: the Windows block's SwiftShader data_deps honour enable_swiftshader (unchanged where it is true). With
  dawn_use_swiftshader = false in venetium/args/out-arm-rt21.gn, SwiftShader leaves the ARM graph (gn gen 38,240 -> 38,183
  targets; the 2 SwiftShader objects that failed are no longer built).
- third_party/cpuinfo/BUILD.gn, src/src/cpuinfo/internal-api.h, src/src/arm/windows/init.c: Windows ARM32 uses the Windows-on-Arm
  init (registry MIDR, GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx topology) and set_cpuinfo_isa_fields reports only the ARMv7 baseline the
  Microsoft ARM32 ABI guarantees (Thumb-2, VFPv3-D32, NEON). chrome reaches cpuinfo through TFLite/ruy (webrtc, services/audio,
  webnn, ...) even with use_on_device_model_service = false. init.c is CRLF upstream and stays CRLF: this patch carries CRLF lines
  for it, so git apply keeps them both ways (it was captured with GIT_ATTR_SOURCE=<empty tree>, because .gitattributes says
  "*.c text eol=lf"; applying needs nothing special).
- chrome/installer/util/additional_parameters.cc: kArchSuffix L"-arch_arm", stable L"stable-arch_arm" (cosmetic; Venetium does not
  use Google Update).
- chrome/browser/component_updater/soda_component_installer.cc: kSodaIndicatorFile "SODAFiles/arch_arm" (compiles; no ARM32 SODA).
Every hunk leaves Windows x86, x64 and arm64 and Linux/Android ARM32 unchanged (reviewed by four read-only lenses before capture).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph after gn gen): the 15 remaining failed objects and cpuinfo's 3 ARM objects compile, 0 FAILED;
the ARM objects are ARMNT, the snapshot-toolchain paint_vector_icon.obj is I386; no object references _MulUnsignedHigh.

rt2.1-fix v2: the fxdiv.h hunk (B3 -> LLVM 0012) and the Skia pcs hunk (pcs -> LLVM 0014) are dropped.

